    "question": "To make a cherry pie, Veronica needs 3 pounds of pitted cherries.  There are 80 single cherries in one pound of cherries.   It takes 10 minutes to pit 20 cherries.  How many hours will it take Veronica to pit all the cherries?",
    "gold": "2",
    "answer": "There are 80 cherries in a pound and she needs 3 pounds to make a pie so she needs 80*3 = <<80*3=240>>240 cherries\nIt takes her 10 minutes to pit a unit of 20 cherries. She has 240/20 = <<240/20=12>>12 units of cherries to pit\nIt takes 10 minutes to pit a unit of cherries and she has 12 units so it will take her 10*12 = <<10*12=120>>120 minutes\n60 minutes are in 1 hour and it takes her 120 minutes so that’s 120/60 = <<120/60=2>>2 hours\n#### 2"
  },
  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine how long it will take Veronica to pit all the cherries, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the total number of cherries Veronica needs.\n2. Determine the total time required to pit all the cherries.\n3. Convert the total time from minutes to hours.\n\n**Step 1: Calculate the total number of cherries.**\n\nVeronica needs 3 pounds of pitted cherries. Since there are 80 cherries in one pound, the total number of cherries is:\n\\[ 3 \\text{ pounds} \\times 80 \\text{ cherries per pound} = 240 \\text{ cherries} \\]\n\n**Step 2: Determine the total time required to pit all the cherries.**\n\nIt takes 10 minutes to pit 20 cherries. Therefore, the time required to pit 1 cherry is:\n\\[ \\frac{10 \\text{ minutes}}{20 \\text{ cherries}} = 0.5 \\text{ minutes per cherry} \\]\n\nThe total time required to pit 240 cherries is:\n\\[ 240 \\text{ cherries} \\times 0.5 \\text{ minutes per cherry} = 120 \\text{ minutes} \\]\n\n**Step 3: Convert the total time from minutes to hours.**\n\nSince there are 60 minutes in an hour, the total time in hours is:\n\\[ \\frac{120 \\text{ minutes}}{60 \\text{ minutes per hour}} = 2 \\text{ hours} \\]\n\nTherefore, the time it will take Veronica to pit all the cherries is \\(\\boxed{2}\\).",
